    {
      "id": "44115956",
      "title": "Chaining Pipes & Being Aware of Limitations",
      "lectureOrder": 170,
      "videoOrder": 162,
      "sourceHash": "670dd03f9fe9bd93614bd4f0a43c32c242d2d6031794701a7f79723b6671a205",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "Now when working with pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 4.62,
          "en": "you sometimes have a scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.62,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "where pipes should be combined, like here, where I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "to format both the decimal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 15.74,
          "en": "as well as my temperature output style and the conversion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 19.35,
          "en": "And you can combine pipes by simply chaining them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.35,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "after each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 23.67,
          "en": "So here I could add another pipe symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 26.887,
          "en": "and then first use the number pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.887,
          "end": 30.84,
          "en": "and then thereafter the temperature pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.84,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "Now, one problem I'll face here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "is that the number pipe actually returns a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "of string or null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "And my temperature pipe only accepts input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 45.12,
          "en": "that are strings or numbers, not null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.12,
          "end": 47.67,
          "en": "So therefore, here I wanna make that pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.67,
          "end": 51.167,
          "en": "my custom pipe a bit more flexible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.167,
          "end": 53.343,
          "en": "by also accepting a null value as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 57.51,
          "en": "which then just also means that I need to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.51,
          "end": 60.333,
          "en": "for a scenario where my value is null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.23,
          "end": 64.953,
          "en": "So therefore, here I'll check if not value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.94,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "So if it is not defined or if it is null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "And in that case, I'll just return that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "instead of trying to format it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "because there is no value anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "But with that change made, we can chain the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 82.893,
          "en": "and temp pipe, and now the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.893,
          "end": 85.607,
          "en": "for the temp pipe will simply be the output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.607,
          "end": 88.08,
          "en": "of the number pipe, which in turn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.08,
          "end": 90.84,
          "en": "takes this value as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "So the output of the number pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 93.96000000000001,
          "en": "is the input of the temp pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.96000000000001,
          "end": 96.09,
          "en": "And therefore, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.09,
          "end": 99.09,
          "en": "I still get a strange output here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.09,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "though not the same output as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 104.43,
          "en": "Well, here it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.43,
          "end": 106.89,
          "en": "that we got a different output than before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.89,
          "end": 111,
          "en": "because the number pipe in the end truncated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 112.5,
          "en": "that input value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.5,
          "end": 114.66,
          "en": "So just to make clear that we're on the same page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.66,
          "end": 119.55,
          "en": "if I remove that decimal pipe, I got this value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.55,
          "end": 122.19,
          "en": "as an output of my custom pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.19,
          "end": 124.207,
          "en": "And with the decimal pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.207,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "I got a slightly different number output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "And that's happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 132,
          "en": "because the decimal pipe changes the input number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132,
          "end": 133.14,
          "en": "it truncates it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 135.36,
          "en": "and it's then this truncated number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.36,
          "end": 137.253,
          "en": "that's passed into the temp pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 140.79,
          "en": "But one problem that remains with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.79,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "is that we potentially get a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "as an input that leads to a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 148.77,
          "en": "with lots of decimal places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 151.17000000000002,
          "en": "And the decimal pipe can't help us here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.17000000000002,
          "end": 154.07,
          "en": "because it can't transform the output of the temp pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.07,
          "end": 157.35,
          "en": "because it doesn't know how to work with a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.35,
          "end": 160.983,
          "en": "that has such a temperature symbol in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.94,
          "end": 165.06,
          "en": "So therefore, here, whilst we can chain pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 167.04,
          "en": "this is not really a solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.04,
          "end": 170.67000000000002,
          "en": "that helps us without putting this number in a nicer way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.67000000000002,
          "end": 175.17000000000002,
          "en": "And it is important to understand that you can combine pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.17000000000002,
          "end": 177.78,
          "en": "with each other, that you can chain them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.78,
          "end": 181.56,
          "en": "but that this approach still can have limits.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.56,
          "end": 182.583,
          "en": "And therefore, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 183.97,
          "end": 185.01,
          "en": "I actually don't wanna chain these pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 185.01,
          "end": 188.64,
          "en": "Instead, I'll simply tweak my temperature pipe code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.64,
          "end": 190.56,
          "en": "and there make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 190.56,
          "end": 194.1,
          "en": "that when I output my output temperature down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 194.1,
          "end": 198.48,
          "en": "at the end, I call the built in two fixed method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 198.48,
          "end": 201.573,
          "en": "and make sure that I only output two decimal places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 204.78,
          "en": "That's the cleaner approach here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.78,
          "end": 208.71,
          "en": "But I wanted to show you how you could chain pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.71,
          "end": 210.63,
          "en": "because it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 210.63,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "that you can do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 214.56,
          "en": "even though it would not be the right solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 214.56,
          "end": 216.9,
          "en": "in this case, or to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 216.9,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "it would not give us the desired result here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 221.43,
          "en": "We could have changed the pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 221.43,
          "end": 224.91,
          "en": "but here the result would've been kind of wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 224.91,
          "end": 228.72,
          "en": "Well, and therefore here, now I'll actually adjust this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 228.72,
          "end": 232.26,
          "en": "to convert a Celsius value to Fahrenheit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 232.26,
          "end": 235.98,
          "en": "And I'll then use this here in all these places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 235.98,
          "end": 239.28,
          "en": "instead of the number pipe, in all these places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
